hadiths[29]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1464","Narrated Abu Tha'labah Al-Khushani:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! We are a people who hunt.' He said: 'If you send your dog and you mentioned the Name of Allah upon it"""""
"1465","Abu Kurayb narrated to us: Abu Bakr ibn 'Ayyash narrated to us from 'Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: ""Whoever drinks wine, flog him. If he repeats it a fourth time, kill him."" He said: And in this chapter there are narrations from Abu Hurayrah, al-Sharid, Shurahbil ibn Aws, Jarir, Abu al-Ramad al-Balawi, and 'Abdullah ibn 'Amr. Abu 'Isa said: The hadith of Mu'awiyah was narrated thus by al-Thawri also from 'Asim, from Abu Salih, from Mu'awiyah, from the Prophet ﷺ. And Ibn Jurayj and Ma'mar narrated from Suhayl ibn Abi Salih, from his father, from Abu Hurayrah, from the Prophet ﷺ. I heard Muhammad say: The hadith of Abu Salih from Mu'awiyah from the Prophet ﷺ in this matter is more authentic than the hadith of Abu Salih from Abu Hurayrah from the Prophet ﷺ. And this was only in the beginning, then it was abrogated later. Thus Muhammad ibn Ishaq narrated from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: ""Whoever drinks wine, flog him. If he repeats it a fourth time, kill him."" He said: Then the Prophet ﷺ was brought a man who had drunk wine for the fourth time after that, so he flogged him but did not kill him. And al-Zuhri narrated similarly from Qabisah ibn Dhu'ayb, from the Prophet ﷺ. He said: So the killing was lifted, and it was a concession. And the practice is according to this hadith among the majority of the people of knowledge; we know no difference of opinion among them in that, whether early or late. And what strengthens this is what was narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through many chains that he said: ""The blood of a Muslim man who testifies that there is no god but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful except for one of three: a life for a life, the married adulterer, and the one who leaves his religion."""""
"1466","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the game caught by a falcon. So he said: 'What it catches for you"""""
"1467","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! I shoot some game and then find my arrow in it the next day.' He said: 'If you know that your arrow killed it"""""
"1468","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about hunting"""""
"1469","Narrated 'Adi bin Hatim:\I asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about the game caught by a trained dog. He said: 'If you mention the Name of Allah when you send your trained dog"""""
"1470","Narrated Jabir bin 'Abdullah:That a man from his people hunted a rabbit or two and slaughtered them with Marwah. Then he hung them up until he met the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)"
"1471","Narrated Abu Ad-Darda':\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited eating the Mujath-thamah"""""
"1472","Narrated Umm Habibah bint Al-'Irbad:From her father: \On the day of Khaibar"""""
"1473","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) prohibited taking a living thing as a shooting target"""""
"1474","Narrated Abu Sa'eed:That the Prophet (ﷺ) said: \Slaughtering the fetus is (achieved by) the slaughtering of its mother"""""
"1475","Narrated to us Muhammad ibn al-Yahya al-Naysaburi: narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yusuf, from Isra'il, narrated to us Simak ibn Harb, from 'Alqamah ibn Wa'il al-Kindi, from his father, that a woman went out during the time of the Messenger of Allah ﷺ intending to pray. A man encountered her, overpowered her, and satisfied his need from her. She cried out and fled. Another man passed by her, and she said, \That man did such-and-such to me.\"" She then passed by a group of the Muhajirun and said"
"1476","Narrated Abu Hurairah:\The Prophet (ﷺ) prohibited every predator that possesses canine teeth"""""
"1477","Narrated Abu Al-'Ushara':From his father that he said: \I said: 'O Messenger of Allah! Is there no slaughtering except upon the neck and the throat ?' He said: 'If you stab its thigh it would be accepted to you"""""
"1478","Narrated Abu Hurairah:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever kills a gecko in one strike"""""
"1479","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Kill snakes and kill Dhut-Tufyatain and Al-Abtar"""""
"1480","Narrated Abu Laila:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \When a snake appears in your dwellings then say to it: We ask you - by covenant of Nuh"""""
"1481","Abu Kurayb and Abu al-Sa’ib Salm ibn Junadah both narrated to us: Abu Usamah narrated to us, from Burayd ibn ‘Abdullah ibn Abi Burdah, from his grandfather Abu Burdah, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “Whoever takes up arms against us is not one of us.” (Al-Tirmidhi said:) There are narrations on this topic from Ibn ‘Umar, Ibn al-Zubayr, Abu Hurayrah, and Salamah ibn al-Akwa‘. The hadith of Abu Musa is hasan sahih."
"1482","Ahmad ibn Mani‘ narrated to us: Abu Mu‘awiyah narrated to us, from Isma‘il ibn Muslim, from al-Hasan, from Jundub, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “The punishment for the sorcerer is a strike of the sword.” Abu ‘Isa said: This hadith is not known as marfu‘ (attributed to the Prophet ﷺ) except through this chain. Isma‘il ibn Muslim al-Makki is considered weak in hadith, while Isma‘il ibn Muslim al-‘Abdi al-Basri is deemed trustworthy by Waki‘. This narration is also reported from al-Hasan, but the correct version from Jundub is mawquf (stopped at the Companion). \nThis hadith is acted upon by some scholars among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others, and it is the view of Malik ibn Anas. Al-Shafi‘i said: “The sorcerer is only killed if his sorcery reaches the level of disbelief (kufr). If his act falls short of disbelief, we do not prescribe execution.”"
"1483","Muhammad ibn ‘Amr al-Sawwaq narrated to us: ‘Abd al-‘Aziz ibn Muhammad narrated to us, from Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, from Salim ibn ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar, from ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Umar, from ‘Umar, that the Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “Whoever you find committing ghulul (embezzlement) in the cause of Allah, burn his belongings.” Salih said: I visited Maslamah, and Salim ibn ‘Abdullah was with him. A man was found to have committed ghulul, so Salim narrated this hadith, and Maslamah ordered the man’s belongings to be burned. Among his possessions, a mushaf (copy of the Qur’an) was found. Salim said: “Sell this and give its price in charity.” \nAbu ‘Isa said: This hadith is gharib; we do not know it except through this chain. This is the practice followed by some scholars, and it is the view of al-Awza‘i, Ahmad, and Ishaq. I asked Muhammad (i.e., al-Bukhari) about this hadith, and he said: “This was narrated only by Salih ibn Muhammad ibn Zaidah, also known as Abu Waqid al-Laythi, who is considered munkar (rejected) in hadith.” Muhammad added: “In other narrations from the Prophet ﷺ regarding the ghulul, he did not command the burning of the offender’s belongings.” Abu ‘Isa said: This is a gharib hadith."
"1484","Muhammad ibn Rafi‘ narrated to us: Ibn Abi Fudayk narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Isma‘il ibn Abi Habibah, from Dawud ibn al-Husayn, from ‘Ikrimah, from Ibn ‘Abbas, from the Prophet ﷺ, who said: “If a man says to another, ‘O Jew,’ strike him twenty lashes; and if he says, ‘O effeminate one,’ strike him twenty lashes; and whoever commits incest with a mahram relative, kill him.” \nAbu ‘Isa said: This hadith is not known except through this chain. Ibrahim ibn Isma‘il is considered weak in hadith. This is the practice followed by our companions, who said: “Whoever commits incest with a mahram relative, knowing it, is subject to execution.” Ahmad said: “Whoever marries his mother is to be killed.” Ishaq said: “Whoever commits incest with a mahram relative is to be killed.” \nIt is also narrated from the Prophet ﷺ through other chains, reported by al-Bara’ ibn ‘Azib and Qurrah ibn Iyas al-Muzani, that a man married his father’s wife, and the Prophet ﷺ ordered his execution."
"1485","Qutaybah narrated to us: al-Layth narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Habib, from Bukayr ibn ‘Abdullah ibn al-Ashaj, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, who said: The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said: “No one should be flogged more than ten lashes except in one of the prescribed punishments (hudud) of Allah.” \nAbu ‘Isa said: This is a hasan gharib hadith; we do not know it except from the narration of Bukayr ibn al-Ashaj. Scholars have differed regarding ta‘zir (discretionary punishment), and the best narration on this matter is this hadith. \nThis hadith was also narrated by Ibn Lahi‘ah from Bukayr, but he made an error, saying: “From ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah, from his father, from the Prophet ﷺ”—and this is incorrect. The correct version is the hadith of Layth ibn Sa‘d: it is ‘Abd al-Rahman ibn Jabir ibn ‘Abdullah, from Abu Burdah ibn Niyar, from the Prophet ﷺ."
"1486","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Kill snakes and kill Dhut-Tufyatain and Al-Abtar"""""
"1487","Narrated by ʿAdiyy ibn Ḥātim (may Allāh be pleased with him):\n\nHe said: \I said"
"1488","then kill them. \\nJam e Tirmazi Hadees: 1484 Arabic Hadees: 1484\"" 1489"""""
"1489","Yusuf ibn 'Isa narrated to us: Waki' narrated to us: Sharik narrated to us from al-Hajjaj, from al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah, from Sulayman al-Yashkuri, from Jabir ibn 'Abdullah, who said: We were forbidden from hunting with the dog of the Magians. Abu 'Isa said: This is a gharib hadith; we know it only from this face (chain). And the practice is according to this among the majority of the people of knowledge; they do not permit hunting with the dog of the Magians. And al-Qasim ibn Abi Bazzah is al-Qasim ibn Nafi' al-Makki."
"1490","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mughaffal:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \If it were not that dogs were part of a nation among the nations"""""
"1491","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:That the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: \Whoever keeps a dog\"" - or: \""acquires a dog\"" - \""neither of hunting nor to guard livestock"""""
"1492","Narrated Ibn 'Umar:\The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered killing dogs"""""
